Description: pkg upgrade of NextBSD packages goes into a new boot environment
 On a ZFS install, an upgrade that changes anything from the NextBSD
 repository is not applied to the running system. pkg asks
 /usr/libexec/nextbsd/bootenv-update to clone the running boot environment
 (begin), runs itself again as pkg -r <clone> with the same arguments, and
 on success has the clone named after the version in it and made the next
 system to start (commit); on failure or a "no" at the prompt the clone is
 removed (abort). Update.app does the same through SettingsHelper.
 .
 Upgrades from other repositories only, UFS installs (bootenv-update check
 fails), pkg -r/-c/-j, -n, -F and NEXTBSD_PKG_IN_PLACE in the environment all
 upgrade in place as upstream does.
Origin: NextBSD
Bug: https://github.com/nextbsd/nextbsd/issues/703
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
